= Pragmatics — Simple =

'''Pragmatics''' is about how people understand language in real situations.

The words in a sentence do not always tell you everything the speaker means. You may also need to know who is speaking, what happened earlier, what both people know, and what the speaker is trying to do.

For example, “It is cold in here” can be a simple statement. In another situation it can also be a request to close a window.

[[Semantics/Simple|Semantics]] studies meaning. Pragmatics focuses especially on meaning in use and on [[Context (linguistics)/Simple|context]].

Important pragmatic ideas include [[Presupposition/Simple|presupposition]], [[Implicature/Simple|implicature]], [[Speech act/Simple|speech acts]], and [[Common ground/Simple|common ground]].

